{"id": "EUVD-2026-103013", "enisaUuid": "cd908bb4-be9a-30ab-ac5a-b217203a0756", "description": "Open WES through 1.0.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows authenticated users to modify other warehouses' stock records because GlobalGatewayFilter never enforces auth_warehouse scoping. Attackers holding the menu permission can enumerate sequential IDs on freezeContainerStock and unfreezeContainerStock endpoints to freeze or unfreeze container stock in other warehouses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:40:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:16:25", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/open-wes-gateway-missing-warehouse-scope-authz", "https://github.com/jingsewu/open-wes/blob/v1.0.0/server/modules-gateway/gateway-core/src/main/java/org/openwes/gateway/filter/GlobalGatewayFilter.java#L86-L128", "https://github.com/jingsewu/open-wes/blob/v1.0.0/server/modules-wes/wes-stock/src/main/java/org/openwes/wes/stock/controller/ContainerStockController.java#L24-L34", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/open-wes-through-1.0.0-broken-access-control-via-globalgatewayfilter-warehouse-scoping"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5ww9-qwj2-mr7g", "CVE-2026-111721"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e3d80f20-060e-3944-a823-3e68f3b101c5", "product": {"name": "open-wes", "vendor": {"name": "jingsewu"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e23328d9-8533-34fd-85d4-28e2dbea994e", "vendor": {"name": "jingsewu"}}], "isExploited": false}